      "full_text": "NYC expert. I have been published in The New York Times, Boston Magazine, Time Out NY For Kids, New England Travel & Life, The Boston Herald, Woman\u2019s Day, Parenting, The New York Daily News, The New York Post, Travel Agent Magazine, Business Travel News, Restaurant Business, Travelmuse.com, Nearsay.com, Care.com and many more. As a contributing writer to TravelChannel.com, I was the site\u2019s NYC expert. I have also written essays for Working Mother magazine, Salon.com and Sesame Street Parents . I have blogged at GM\u2019s drivethedistrict.com, The Otesaga Resort in Cooperstown, Travelmuse.com and Nearsay.com. As a travel editor for ten years at Bridal Guide, a national glossy bridal magazine in NYC, I assigned, wrote and edited hundreds of articles that revolved around honeymoons and destination weddings. I traveled extensively to various honeymoon destinations across the globe from tropical islands like Bora-Bora and Maldives to cultural hubs such as Paris and Rome. In addition to my work in print media, digital platforms have been a significant part of my career evolution; blogging has allowed me an intimate connection with readers who seek authentic travel experiences. My blog covers everything New York City\u2014from the best hidden gems for foodies like myself (with vegan options always on radar) down to family-friendly activities that keep kids engaged and parents relaxed. I am passionate about storytelling, which is evident in my two published books: \"NYC Unveiled,\" a guidebook offering unique insights into lesser-known attractions around New York City; and \u201cTaste of Home,\u201d an anthology where I explore the culinary landscapes through p",
